course: dictionary
lesson: 11401
title: The helper in the wrong deed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An accomplice is a person who helps someone else do something wrong or commit a crime. You can find the meaning in the words around it. Ask yourself who is helping and what the wrong thing is.
explain: «The thief picked the lock, and his accomplice kept watch by the door.» The thief did the main wrong deed. His accomplice helped by watching for people who might catch them. Swap in the word helper and check: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The accomplice does not have to do the main wrong thing to be part of it. «Mia laughed while Tom hid Sam's bag, but she was his accomplice in the trick.» Mia did not hide the bag herself, but she helped, so she is part of the wrong deed too.
fact: An accomplice is a person who helps someone else do something wrong or commit a crime.
fact: «His accomplice» means the helper of that particular person, as in «the robber and his accomplice».
fact: The phrase «an accomplice in» is followed by the wrong thing, as in «an accomplice in the cheating».
fact: In law, an accomplice can be punished too, even if they did not do the main wrong thing themselves.
fact: Stories, detective books and the news often use this word for the helper who keeps watch or drives the car.
exercise: «The thief picked the lock, and his accomplice kept watch by the door.» Who is the accomplice? | The lock on the door | The police officer | *The person who helped the thief by keeping watch
exercise: Ben said, «I did not hide the teacher's pen, but I helped Jay do it, so I was his accomplice.» What is an accomplice? | *A person who helps someone else do something wrong | A teacher who gives out pens | A friend who only plays football
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a helper in a crime: «The robbers escaped, and their accomplice drove the van.» | van | escaped | *accomplice | robbers
test: «The bank robber waited outside while his accomplice went inside.» What does accomplice mean here? | *Someone who helps the robber commit the crime | A bank customer | A police officer
test: Sara said, «Nobody saw me, but I was the accomplice when Lily broke the window.» What does accomplice mean? | A person who fixed the window | A person who saw the crime | A person who called the police | *A person who helped someone do something wrong
exam: Which sentence shows an accomplice? | *The robber's friend kept watch outside while he stole the jewels | The cat sat by the fire all afternoon | Ella baked a cake for her gran | The teacher helped the class finish the project
